Step-by-Step Algorithm:

Initialize Dimensions
Let n be the number of rows in the matrix.
Let m be the number of columns in the matrix.

Create Marker Arrays
Create a boolean array r of size n to track rows that must be set to zero.
Create a boolean array c of size m to track columns that must be set to zero.

First Pass – Identify Zero Positions
Traverse the matrix using two nested loops.
For each element at position (i, j):
If the element is 0:
Mark r[i] = true
Mark c[j] = true

Second Pass – Update Matrix
Traverse the matrix again using two nested loops.
For each element at position (i, j):
If r[i] is true or c[j] is true:
Set matrix[i][j] = 0

End
The matrix is now modified in-place with required rows and columns set to zero.

Time Complexity
First traversal of matrix: O(n × m)
Second traversal of matrix: O(n × m)
Total Time Complexity:
O(n×m)

Space Complexity
Boolean array for rows: O(n)
Boolean array for columns: O(m)
Total Space Complexity:
O(n+m)



